task: ui-mobile
agent: fable-frontend
started: 2026-09-09
branch: feature/ui-mobile
worktree: ../okay-wt-ui-mobile
spec: specs/frontend.md — a new section "Mobile", written by this claim

why: the operator's next direction (2026-09-09): mobile frontends and
  applications, web and native, on top of the landed arc.

what: three lanes in order, each measured. M1 mobile web: Live pages
  become installable, mobile-first pages (viewport, level-L CSS with
  tap-sized controls, a web manifest, a service worker caching the
  shell so the SSR'd page opens offline), proved with Playwright in
  an iPhone emulation through the e2e harness. M2 iOS: a SwiftPM
  package (protocol + SwiftUI level L + URLSession WebSocket client)
  with the conformance test under `swift test`, compiled for the iOS
  simulator SDK. M3 Android: the SDK by brew + sdkmanager, an
  androidTarget on okay-compose, a debug APK built.

predict: M1 a day's worth of CSS/JS in an hour; M2 the Kotlin client
  transcribed; M3 gated by the box's memory and the SDK download.
